timing in a cultivar specific manner. Frost exposure decreases when bloom occurs after peak

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:37.920
risk periods. Next, marine ecology. University of Sydney findings challenged the view of these

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:44.080
starfish as solely destructive. Controlled populations raised coral prevalence and species richness

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:50.660
on reefs. The study measured outcomes after targeted density adjustments. Positive effects emerged

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:56.760
under specific management conditions. Starfish grazing can reduce competitive dominance among coral

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:03.520
species. Diversity gains appeared at intermediate population levels. On education and technology,

