00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.240
Finally, materials and atmospheric science.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:09.000
New experiments demonstrate ice nucleation proceeds through previously unrecognized pathways.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.960
studies. The work alters understanding of how ice crystals initiate in natural settings.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.020
Results carry implications for atmospheric science and cryopreservation techniques.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:23.800
Surface interactions and impurities play larger roles than previously modeled.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:30.020
Homogeneous nucleation requires far lower temperatures than heterogeneous cases. Revised

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:34.060
models may improve predictions in both climate and preservation contexts.

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:34.240
