00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:40.140
The REM sleep study tracked objective sleep architecture across more than 95,000 adults.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:45.780
Greater time in REM stage associated with lower incidence of 83 distinct conditions.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.660
Deep sleep showed separate protective associations with metabolic and mood disorders.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:55.940
These patterns emerged after accounting for total sleep duration and other covariates.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:08:01.640
The scale of the cohort allows detection of modest effect sizes across many diagnoses.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:07.360
One open question is whether interventions that extend REM sleep can shift disease trajectories

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:12.820
in at-risk groups. Objective recordings provided the primary data rather than questionnaire

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:18.900
responses. Most people assume ice forms when water simply reaches zero degrees Celsius and

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:24.840
molecules slow enough to lock into place. That picture misses the actual trigger. Right now,

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:31.140
as water vapor or liquid sits in clouds or biological tissues, ice starts only when a rare

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:34.300
nucleation event creates the first stable crystal lattice.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:39.540
A single successful nucleus can then propagate rapidly through surrounding molecules.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:45.580
Recent experiments at Boise State quantified how surface chemistry and impurities lower

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.580
the energy barrier far below textbook expectations.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:55.260
The memorable detail is that homogeneous nucleation in pure water requires temperatures near minus

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:00.420
40 degrees Celsius, while everyday surfaces allow freezing at much warmer readings.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:06.100
Listeners can watch for updated atmospheric models that incorporate these revised nucleation

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:09.060
rates when forecasting precipitation or frost events.

